s or\n  documentation that directly fall out of these changes (incidental\n  touch-ups only — no new documentation content).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the project creation flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n  control is unreachable.\n- Given the workbench spawn flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n  control is unreachable.\n- Given the model deployment flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n  control is unreachable.\n- Given the pipeline run submission flow, when it is operated end to end using\n  only the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs,\n  and no control is unreachable.\n- Given the interactive controls across the four audited flows, when an\n  element receives keyboard focus, then a visible focus indicator is shown\n  with a consistent treatment across all four flows.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is addressed\n  or explicitly dispositioned with rationale in the epic's completion record.\n- The existing automated test suite passes and the Dashboard's existing build\n  pipeline is green with these changes; keyboard fixes do not regress\n  pointer-based interaction in the four flows.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by\n  keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by this\n  epic's flow-by-flow keyboard operability acceptance criteria.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the\n  audited flows: covered by this epic's consistent focus-indicator scope and\n  acceptance criterion.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33189,"output_tokens":0},"context