{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c95b29724cd9da6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects found by the\n34\taccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation,\n35\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion,\n36\teach of the four flows can be completed end to end with keyboard alone — no\n37\tfocus traps, no unreachable controls — and visible focus indicators are\n38\tconsistent across the audited flows. This delivers the code-side half of the\n39\tstrategy's keyboard conformance work; the updated conformance documentation\n40\tthat reflects this fixed state is delivered separately.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Remediate every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit report for the\n45\t  four audited flows, including:\n46\t  - focus loss and focus traps in modals opened during the flows;\n47\t  - controls that are unreachable via keyboard (cannot be focused or activated\n48\t    without a pointer);\n49\t  - inconsistent or missing visible focus indicators on interactive controls.\n50\t- Make each of the four flows fully operable by keyboard alone, from entry\n51\t  through completion of the flow, including cancel/dismiss paths.\n52\t- Apply a consistent focus-indicator treatment across the audited flows'\n53\t  interactive controls so focus state is visibly uniform.\n54\t- Keep the fixes within the four audited flows and within keyboard-related\n55\t  behavior: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\n56\t  and flows outside the four audited ones, are out of scope per the strategy.\n57\t- Update any screenshots, captions, or references in existing test fixtures or\n58\t  documentation that directly fall out of these changes (incidental\n59\t  touch-ups only — no new documentation content).\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given the project creation flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n64\t  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n65\t  control is unreachable.\n66\t- Given the workbench spawn flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n67\t  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n68\t  control is unreachable.\n69\t- Given the model deployment flow, when it is operated end to end using only\n70\t  the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs, and no\n71\t  control is unreachable.\n72\t- Given the pipeline run submission flow, when it is operated end to end using\n73\t  only the keyboard, then every step can be completed, no focus trap occurs,\n74\t  and no control is unreachable.\n75\t- Given the interactive controls across the four audited flows, when an\n76\t  element receives keyboard focus, then a visible focus indicator is shown\n77\t  with a consistent treatment across all four flows.\n78\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is addressed\n79\t  or explicitly dispositioned with rationale in the epic's completion record.\n80\t- The existing automated test suite passes and the Dashboard's existing build\n81\t  pipeline is green with these changes; keyboard fixes do not regress\n82\t  pointer-based interaction in the four flows.\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by\n87\t  keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by this\n88\t  epic's flow-by-flow keyboard operability acceptance criteria.\n89\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the\n90\t  audited flows: covered by this epic's consistent focus-indicator scope and\n91\t  acceptance criterion.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae533f120c3d1f3a","agent_id":"a70d72158ffcde1e6","session_id":"30454257-140a-49db-af81-5209d36a12cc","uuid":"55304c28-22e9-4169-a48f-d563d92f694c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:17:16.230Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c95b29724cd9da6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
