{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98926822ef220ed3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Epic Boundaries\n9\t  description: E001 spans four flows with no size estimate or conditional re-split\n10\t    trigger recorded; record the estimate and the per-flow re-split trigger (e.g.\n11\t    defect volume or elapsed time exceeding one sprint) in Health Warnings or the\n12\t    epic body\n13\terror: null\n14\t---\n15\t## Review Summary\n16\t\n17\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n18\tRecommendation: accept\n19\t\n20\tContract validator: OK (`skills/epic-decompose/scripts/validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-9017` exited 0 — body sections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance, implementation-type parallelism, and shared-surface enforcement all pass).\n21\t\n22\tTriage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 2 epics — consistent; multi-epic output is expected for a full decomposition. The Step 0 escape (multiple work streams: Dashboard code remediation + substantive docs authoring) is correctly justified in the summary.\n23\t\n24\t## Criterion Details\n25\t\n26\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n27\tAll three HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 (P1) and HLR-2 (P1) → E001, HLR-3 (P2) → E002. The traceability matrix is present in the decomposition summary and each epic carries an HLR Traceability section matching it. Priority inheritance is sound: E001 (P1) blocks only E002 (P2) — the prerequisite is higher priority than the work it enables, and E002 is a `docs-authoring` epic whose P2 derives from the strategy's Normal Jira priority (exempt from inheritance). No priority collapse: HLR-1 and HLR-2 are both P1 and remediate the same audit findings over the same four flow surfaces; the summary explicitly records why they are not split, which is the correct shape.\n28\t\n29\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n30\tSingle edge E001 → E002 matches E002's frontmatter `dependencies: [RHAISTRAT-9017-E001]` exactly, and the diagram arrow direction (dependency → dependent) is correct. The edge is a valid Rule 11 edge (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics) and does not trigger priority inheritance. No circular dependencies, no invalid edges, no branch files. Critical path length 2 fits the S-strategy heuristic (1-2). No konflux-onboarding or license-validation epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not engaged. Cross-check for missing edges: E002's content is fully determined by E001's outcome and the edge exists; no other epic content implies an uncaptured data/artifact dependency. Validator confirms DAG consistency.\n31\t\n32\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n33\tE001 (Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard) and E002 (Documentation / RHOAI Documentation) are separate epics along the component/team boundary — correct. Work-product types are properly separated: E001 is code implementation only (\"incidental touch-ups only — no new documentation content\"), E002 is content authoring only. No scope duplication: no epic rebuilds another's surface. One watch item (minor): E001 spans four flows and carries no size estimate or conditional re-split trigger in the epic body or Health Warnings. It is one logical change (same three defect classes, audit-enumerated targets, shared focus-indicator treatment), so a split is not demanded, but the natural seam (per-flow) should be recorded as a re-split trigger in case the audit defect volume pushes it past a sprint. A single minor does not reduce the score.\n34\t\n35\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n36\tBoth epics are Implementation and both produce concrete artifacts (remediated Dashboard code; republished VPAT and accessibility statement). No Investigation epics — correctly so, since the strategy states there are no open questions and the audit enumerates the exact defects. No `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are set and none are required (no gates exist).\n37\t\n38\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n39\tBoth epics are Implementation and carry `ai_signals` (not `investigation_signals`) — type-appropriate. Both ai-signals files exist and their rationales match the frontmatter values. E001's values are well justified against the strategy (audit-enumerated defects → change_specificity 1; remediation of shipped flows → existing_foundation 1; \"None\" open questions → open_questions 1). The `architecture_claims: 1` calibration is verified against `.context`: `architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` describes the Dashboard as the single-pane console surfacing projects, workbenches, model serving, and pipelines — corroborating the strategy's premise, and the rationale cites it. E002's `architecture_claims: 0` is correct: no architecture-context file covers the Documentation component (confirmed — only dashboard.md exists in rhoai-3.0), so there is nothing to corroborate. E002's `human_process_gates: -1` is justified by HLR-3's mandated technical review of conformance claims. No arithmetic or threshold checks performed (pipeline-computed).\n40\t\n41\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n42\tE001 has seven testable Given/When/Then ACs covering each of the four flows individually, the consistent focus-indicator treatment, audit-defect disposition, and build-pipeline green with no pointer-interaction regression. E002 has four testable ACs including the Rule-mandated technical review AC for docs-authoring. The externally-controlled renewal schedule is correctly recorded in E002's Risks/Notes rather than as an AC — the canonical soft-AC mistake was avoided. No rollback/feature-flag AC is mandated (remediation, not a replacement). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n43\t\n44\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n45\tAll strategy scope is covered: keyboard operability of the four flows (E001 ACs, one per flow), consistent focus indicators (E001), and VPAT + accessibility statement update, technical review, and republication (E002). The out-of-scope list is respected in both epics' scope sections. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the customer renewal constraint appears in E002's Risks/Notes and the summary's Health Warnings; the audit report as defect source is explicit in E001's scope and ACs; missing strategy sections are disclosed in Health Warnings rather than silently dropped. A docs-authoring epic exists for the documentation deliverable (Rule 11 satisfied). No conditional branches are needed (no bounded outcomes in the strategy).\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd7b0485f03daa1","agent_id":"a725891b31809c23f","session_id":"30454257-140a-49db-af81-5209d36a12cc","uuid":"e3705e58-8d04-408c-b582-65b8b4758ef7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:19:17.845Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98926822ef220ed3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
