{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae38870cdb1a4501","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility conformance for core Dashboard flows\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Normal\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- accessibility\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tAn accessibility audit found that four core Dashboard flows (project creation,\n15\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission) cannot be completed\n16\twith keyboard alone: focus is lost in modals, several controls are unreachable,\n17\tand focus indicators are inconsistent. Two public-sector customers require an\n18\tupdated, published conformance statement (VPAT) before renewal — so the fixes\n19\tand the published documentation are both deliverables of this strategy.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P1 | The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no focus traps or unreachable controls. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows. |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P2 | The accessibility conformance documentation (VPAT and product docs accessibility statement) is updated and republished to reflect the fixed state, with technical review. |\n28\t\n29\t## Affected Components\n30\t\n31\t- Dashboard\n32\t- Documentation\n33\t\n34\t## Out of Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require\n37\t- Flows outside the four audited ones\n38\t\n39\t## Open Questions\n40\t\n41\tNone — the audit report enumerates the exact defects per flow.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd7b0485f03daa1","agent_id":"a725891b31809c23f","session_id":"30454257-140a-49db-af81-5209d36a12cc","uuid":"7e92a1c2-7e5a-470d-81d3-1b12e851cd59","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:19:23.950Z","tool_result_meta":[{"