{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1fb1f92f59d38e5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9017\n11\t\n12\tKeyboard accessibility conformance for core Dashboard flows.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage Outcome\n15\t\n16\tStep 0 Check 1 (below-threshold) does not apply: although the strategy is\n17\tS-sized with no open questions, its scope spans two distinct work streams —\n18\tDashboard code remediation (four flows, keyboard operability and focus\n19\tindicators) and substantive documentation authoring (updated VPAT and product\n20\tdocs accessibility statement, republished). Substantive content authoring is a\n21\tdistinct work stream, so the multiple-work-streams escape condition applies and\n22\tthe strategy proceeds to full decomposition. Check 2 (docs-only) does not\n23\tapply: the Dashboard component requires code changes.\n24\t\n25\t## Epic List\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard accessibility remediation for four core Dashboard flows | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | Update and republish accessibility conformance documentation (VPAT and accessibility statement) | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n31\t\n32\t## Dependency DAG\n33\t\n34\t```mermaid\n35\tgraph TD\n36\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9017-E001: Dashboard keyboard accessibility fixes] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9017-E002: VPAT and accessibility statement update]\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t## DAG Justification\n40\t\n41\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n42\t|------|------|-----------|\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 → RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | The conformance documentation must describe the fixed state of the four flows, so the docs-authoring epic is blocked by the Dashboard implementation epic. E001 is the only other Implementation epic in the strategy. |\n44\t\n45\tNotes on non-edges:\n46\t\n47\t- No Investigation epics: the strategy's Open Questions section states \"None —\n48\t  the audit report enumerates the exact defects per flow\". No conditional ADRs,\n49\t  pending reviews, or genuine unknowns appear elsewhere in the strategy.\n50\t- No onboarding chain: the Dashboard is an existing, Konflux-onboarded\n51\t  component (see `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`),\n52\t  so no `repo-onboarding` / `license-validation` / `konflux-onboarding` epics\n53\t  are generated. The Documentation component has no architecture-context file,\n54\t  but the strategy's Documentation work is an update and republication of\n55\t  already-published documents through the Red Hat docs content process — not\n56\t  provisioning of a new platform component — so no onboarding chain is\n57\t  generated for it either (see Health Warnings).\n58\t- HLR-1 and HLR-2 are both P1 and are kept in a single Dashboard epic: they\n59\t  remediate the same audit findings across the same four flows and the same UI\n60\t  surfaces (modals, controls, focus indicators). Splitting them would have two\n61\t  epics building over the identical flow surfaces — a boundary violation, not\n62\t  a deferral signal.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n65\t\n66\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n67\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n68\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard operability of the four audited flows |\n69\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Consistent visible focus indicators across the audited flows |\n70\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | VPAT and accessibility statement updated, republished, technically reviewed |\n71\t\n72\tAll three HLRs are covered; none is orphaned.\n73\t\n74\t## Health Warnings\n75\t\n76\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n77\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n78\t  Non-Functional Requirements. The Affected Components section is a bare list\n79\t  without change descriptions or owner teams. Decomposition proceeded from the\n80\t  HLR table, problem statement, and out-of-scope list; per-epic acceptance\n81\t  criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n82\t- **Team attribution inferred**: the Dashboard owner team (RHOAI Dashboard) was\n83\t  taken from `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`;\n84\t  the strategy itself names no teams. The Documentation epic is assigned to a\n85\t  documentation team (RHOAI Documentation) as a generic placeholder — confirm\n86\t  the actual owning team before scheduling.\n87\t- **Documentation component not in architecture context**: there is no\n88\t  architecture-context file for Documentation. It is treated as a\n89\t  docs-authoring work stream over already-published documents (the VPAT and\n90\t  accessibility statement exist and are being updated), not as a new platform\n91\t  component requiring provisioning, so no onboarding chain was generated.\n92\t- **Schedule risk (not an AC)**: two public-sector customers require the\n93\t  republished VPAT before renewal. The renewal date is externally controlled\n94\t  and is recorded as a schedule risk on the documentation epic, not as an\n95\t  acceptance criterion.\n96\t- **E001 size estimate and conditional re-split trigger**: E001 spans four\n97\t  flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run\n98\t  submission) and is estimated at roughly one sprint (~10 working days) of\n99\t  Dashboard engineering effort. Why not split: it is one logical change — the\n100\t  same three audit defect classes (modal focus traps, unreachable controls,\n101\t  inconsistent focus indicators) remediated across audit-enumerated targets\n102\t  with a shared focus-indicator treatment; a per-flow split would duplicate\n103\t  the shared treatment and fragment a single audit-remediation pass.\n104\t  Conditional re-split trigger: if the audit defect volume or elapsed effort\n105\t  exceeds one sprint (the epic is not code-complete within a single sprint),\n106\t  split along the per-flow seam into one epic per audited flow, keeping the\n107\t  shared focus-indicator treatment in the first of them.\n108\t- **Component mapping**: both strategy components (Dashboard, Documentation)\n109\t  matched canonical names in `.context/rhai-components.txt` verbatim; no\n110\t  non-obvious mappings were needed.\n111\t\n112\t## Tiered Delivery\n113\t\n114\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n115\tin the Dashboard's own repo plus the Red Hat docs content process.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-97b412119e16a9ff","agent_id":"a76977aa3b935d052","session_id":"30454257-140a-49db-af81-5209d36a12cc","uuid":"216253b9-889b-423f-b95c-21a77c856798","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:20:25.353Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1fb1f92f59d38e5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
